<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  A TEST feed. Not the one the app ships with.

  It exists so the download-and-install path can be exercised before there is a
  release newer than the running build. The payload is the real, signed,
  notarized v1.1.0 disk image; the version it advertises is deliberately absurd
  so that any build offers it.

  Installing from this feed downgrades the app to 1.1.0, which is the point: the
  bytes that arrive are checked against the public key compiled into the running
  build, so a successful install proves the whole chain. Rebuild afterwards.

  Production is appcast.xml. Only a debug build with Pretend Update switched on
  ever reads this file. Delete it once the path is confirmed.
-->
